-- chem/charge.cub — Kirchhoff's electrical-network theory on a graph with unit resistance on every line:
-- spanning trees by Kirchhoff's determinant (1847), effective resistance as a ratio of tree counts, and the
-- least flux energy of a neutral set of point charges (Thomson). This is classical network theory with a
-- chosen weight, and not a derivation from loop quantum gravity. In Thiemann's regularization of the matter
-- Hamiltonian (QSD V, 1997, eq. 3.8) the electric energy is a sum over vertices v and pairs of edges e, e'
-- at v of a weight built from the gravitational volume operator at v times the product of the edges'
-- electric labels; the unit weight here stands where that geometric weight belongs.
import "spin.hypercubical"
